  "notes": "For fresh generation, code selects useful dose from source-owned weekly muscle-volume preferences and movement-development targets. Physical working-set economy follows that dose tier. Standalone source movement balance then optimizes the selected physical workload without adding work. Marked post-workload tiers conserve selected physical work, targeted muscle doses, dose-authorized movement roles and exercise identities. Inclusion-only role counts remain adjustable within their hard coverage and frequency bounds. First prefer the most balanced feasible supported aggregate-muscle exposure, with explicitly targeted regions replacing their parent within that conserved dose. Then prefer fewer native-compatible executed blocks. Remaining selection overlap, direct/supporting overlap, heavy-set balance and similar exercise counts follow. Small unavoidable differences are acceptable; identical exercise counts cannot force poorer muscle distribution. Heavy-exercise-count symmetry, total-set similarity and raw physical preparation counts follow useful grouping and distribution. A balance-only improvement does not authorize added dose. Scales and all hard requirements remain unchanged. The model selects complementary exercises and judges semantic tradeoffs; code owns arithmetic, eligibility, conservation and exact rendering. Unknown physiological fatigue and execution times remain explicit. For an explicitly requested refinement of an accepted reviewed plan, code may preserve that plan's attained per-goal quality through saturated source-approved comparison targets before workload economy, with every underlying preferred range and remaining shortfall still disclosed. Fresh requests never inherit such acceptance from a different conversation. Current source-backed physical setup, capacity and exclusions remain authoritative. Demand-distribution optimization remains suspended. App code owns warm-up construction, calibration and progression. Hip-dominant development has a source-configured soft aspiration of four weekly working sets for this requested program, considered before physical workload minimization. This is not a hard floor or physiological adequacy claim. A bounded numerically promising alternative menu returns to semantic selection before final commitment."
